  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The de-Broglie&#39;s wavelength&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;is Planck&#39;s constant and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;is velocity.</p><p>Using relation between momentum and kinetic energy, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mi>KE</mi></mfenced></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Here, kinetic energy of electron is stated as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>V</mi></math>.</p><p>Then, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>V</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Putting the values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>62</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;of electron</p><p>We get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>22</mn></mrow><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;stand for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>V</mi></msqrt></math>.</p></blockquote>",
